# Parallel projects execution

To speed up test execution, set the `parallelThreads` parameter to the number of Maven processes to run in parallel. When the value ends with "C", the number is multiplied by the number of processors (cores) available to the Java virtual machine.

Example configuration:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-invoker-plugin</artifactId>
        <version>${project.version}</version>
        <configuration>
          <parallelThreads>2C</parallelThreads>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
  ...
</project>
```

# Order of projects execution in parallel mode

In parallel mode, at most `parallelThreads` projects run at any point.

The order in which projects start is **not guaranteed**; most of the time it follows the order in which the file system lists the project directories.

Some projects take longer than others. The next project in the queue starts as soon as a thread is free, so the order of execution can change with the number of processors, the system load and so on.

If you need a defined order, use the `invoker.ordinal` property in [Invoker Properties](./invoker-properties.html).

In parallel mode, projects are **grouped** by `invoker.ordinal`, and the projects of a group run in parallel. The projects of the next group start after all projects of the previous group have finished.

Setup projects always run first, one after the other on a single thread.
